# Frontend env. Copy to .env.local and adjust.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE (browser-side, inlined at build time)
#
# Mode 1, local dev: leave unset (or "/api"). The browser calls the relative
# /api path and next.config.ts rewrites it to BACKEND_ORIGIN. Same origin, so
# no CORS and no token is needed when the backend has none configured.
#
# Mode 2, Vercel against a remote backend: set the absolute backend URL
# including the /api prefix. The console then asks for the API token on
# /login and sends it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (and `?token=` on
# the SSE stream). The backend must allow the Vercel origin in CORS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=/api
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://hq-api.example.com/api

# NEXT_PUBLIC_READER_SYNC_URL (browser-side, public, NOT a secret)
#
# The phone reader (/read) on Vercel: the backend's tailnet origin, so "Mark
# read" and concept taps reach it. No token is sent; Tailscale Serve's
# identity header authenticates the phone. Unset = kept on the phone in an
# outbox. The backend needs this deployment's origin in CORS_ORIGINS.
# See docs/deploy.md section 12.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_READER_SYNC_URL=https://mac.tail1234.ts.net

# Server-only, dev rewrites. next.config.ts rewrites /api/* to this origin.
# Never exposed to the browser. Unused when NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE is absolute.
BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8000
